     1,
     "Hi!<br><br>I&#39;m looking for a solution of a problem in aggregating data by factor.<br><br>I have a dataframe (htpov) with two variables (hab, povrs):<br><span style=\"color:rgb(255,0,0)\"></span><br> <span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">  hab povrs</span><br style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">\n<span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">1  zvo  6837</span><br style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">2  omt  8615</span><br style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">\n<span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">3  omt  1492</span><br style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">4  omt 12978</span><br style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">\n<span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">5 megt 13920</span><br style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">6  omt 19877</span><br>...<br><br>I would like to sum &#39;povrs&#39; for each level of &#39;hab&#39;. <br>\nI tried the function &#39;aggregate&#39;:<br><br><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">htpov.agg&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:courier new,monospace\">aggregate</span><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">(htpov, by=list(hab), FUN=sum, na.rm=T)</span><br>\n<br>But it doesn&#39;t work. As I uderstand, this is because function (FUN) argument must be applicable to all variables in the data set<code></code>?<br>(from decription of the function):<code></code><i><code> FUN</code> ...\n\na scalar function to compute the summary statistics which\ncan be applied to all data subsets. </i><br><br>Since &#39;hab&#39; is a factor, I have a problem ...  <br><br>The Error message:<br><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">Error in Summary.factor(c(1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L), na.rm = TRUE) : </span><br style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">\n<span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">sum not meaningful for factors</span><br><br>I&#39;d appreciate a suggestion about aggregating the data of different types.<br><br>Thanks,<br>Ursa<br><br><br><br>\n"
